%N A400701 Start with a set of five adjacent collinear points in a hexagonal lattice. Every iteration, add to the set the points in the lattice which are adjacent to at least two points already in the set. This sequence gives the number of points in the set after n iterations.
%H A400701 Sean A. Irvine, <a href="/A400701/b400701.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A400701 Aidan Markey, <a href="/A400701/a400701.pdf">Illustration of initial terms</a>
%F A400701 G.f.: (5+3*x+2*x^2-5*x^3+x^4-2*x^5+2*x^6) / ((1-x^3) * (1-x)^2). - _Sean A. Irvine_, Oct 19 2026
%F A400701 a(n) = (3*n^2 + 17*n + 25 - 2*((n-1) mod 3))/3 if n > 1.
%F A400701 Conjectured:
%F A400701 For n > 1: a(n) = A374338(n) + 4*n + 7.
%e A400701 See Links.
%Y A400701 Cf. A374338, A400699, A400700 (corresponding sequences for two, three, and four points).
%Y A400701 Cf. A338097, A400975, A400976, A400977.
